--- !u!114 &2005899136
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2005899134}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3dfb001cd14ff514e9c4dd9236b319be, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::HowToPlay
  titleText: {fileID: 2122720110}
  bodyText: {fileID: 1168514025}
  pageNumberText: {fileID: 175430785}
  previousButton: {fileID: 86435759}
  nextButton: {fileID: 1809979478}
  pages:
  - title: The Goal
    body: 'Work together to get every frog through the level.


      When all the frogs in the game are standing in the level exit, a short countdown starts and everyone moves on to the next level. The HUD shows how many frogs are at the exit.


      Play online with up to 4 players, or offline on your own.'
  - title: Moving
    body: '<b>WASD</b> / <b>Left Stick</b>: hop around

      <b>Mouse</b> / <b>Right Stick</b>: look around

      <b>Mouse Wheel</b>: zoom the camera in and out


      Your frog hops the way you push. Small pushes make small, slow hops.'
  - title: Charge Jump
    body: '<b>Hold Space</b> / <b>A</b> to charge, <b>let go</b> to jump. The longer you hold, the higher and farther you go.


      Hold a direction while charging to aim: your frog turns to face it and leaps that way. Charge without a direction to jump straight up.


      Every jump uses up some hunger, and big jumps use more.'
  - title: Climbing
    body: 'Jump into a climbable wall and your frog grabs on by itself. You can also press <b>E</b> / <b>X</b> next to one.


      <b>WASD</b>: climb up, down and sideways, around corners and over the top

      <b>Space</b> / <b>A</b>: jump off the wall

      <b>E</b> / <b>X</b>: let go and drop


      Your toes can only hold so much. Too much pulling on you (like a teammate hanging on your tongue) and you slip off.'
  - title: Tongue
    body: '<b>Left Click</b> / <b>Right Trigger</b>: shoot your tongue at whatever is under the crosshair


      <b>Flies and food</b>: your tongue reels them in and you eat them, which refills hunger.

      <b>Boxes, objects and frogs</b>: your tongue sticks. Walk away to drag them, and hold <b>Right Click</b> / <b>Left Trigger</b> to reel them closer. Click again to let go.

      <b>Wall buttons</b>: hit them with your tongue to press them.


      <b>Q</b> / <b>B</b>: break free when someone''s tongue is holding you.'
  - title: Staying Alive
    body: '<b>Health</b>: slowly heals while hunger and hydration are both over half full.

      <b>Hunger</b>: goes down when you jump. Eat flies and food to fill it. A hungry frog can''t jump as high.

      <b>Hydration</b>: goes down over time. Catch water drops to fill it. When it runs out you start losing health.


      Some spots in a level refill everything. If your health runs out, you start again with full bars.'
  - title: Teamwork and Puzzles
    body: '<b>Pressure plates</b> open doors while enough weight is on them. Drag boxes onto them with your tongue. Heavy boxes are easier to move together.

      <b>Doors and buttons</b> open for everyone at once.

      <b>Help each other</b>: catch a falling teammate with your tongue, or pull them up a ledge.


      <b>Esc</b> / <b>Start</b>: pause menu. Online, the game keeps going for everyone else while you''re paused.

      <b>Tab</b>: free the mouse without pausing.'
